label: Geomagnetic activity
indices: Kp and Hp30 indices
archive: geomagnetic index archive
summary: Planetary geomagnetic activity index over the time each fix was recorded.
source caveat: Averaged over magnetometer stations worldwide, so a value describes the planet over a period, not the ionosphere above one receiver.
scale caveat: The scale is quasi logarithmic and published in thirds of a unit. Storm levels start at 5 (G1), Kp stops at 9, and Hp30 keeps climbing past it in an extreme storm.
no value caveat: No value was published for this period.
Kp plot hover: Planetary geomagnetic activity, one value per archived 3-hour Kp period across the span the plot shows. Averaged over magnetometer stations worldwide, so a value describes the planet over a period, not the ionosphere above one receiver. The scale is quasi logarithmic and published in thirds of a unit. Storm levels start at 5 (G1), Kp stops at 9, and Hp30 keeps climbing past it in an extreme storm. The line breaks over periods no value is archived for.
Hp30 plot hover: Planetary geomagnetic activity, one value per archived 30-minute Hp30 period across the span the plot shows. Averaged over magnetometer stations worldwide, so a value describes the planet over a period, not the ionosphere above one receiver. The scale is quasi logarithmic and published in thirds of a unit. Storm levels start at 5 (G1), Kp stops at 9, and Hp30 keeps climbing past it in an extreme storm. The line breaks over periods no value is archived for.
Kp query doc: Planetary geomagnetic activity over the 3-hour Kp period the fix's own UTC time falls in. Averaged over magnetometer stations worldwide, so a value describes the planet over a period, not the ionosphere above one receiver. The scale is quasi logarithmic and published in thirds of a unit. Storm levels start at 5 (G1), Kp stops at 9, and Hp30 keeps climbing past it in an extreme storm. Fixes whose day is not in the geomagnetic index archive carry no value.
Hp30 query doc: Planetary geomagnetic activity over the 30-minute Hp30 period the fix's own UTC time falls in. Averaged over magnetometer stations worldwide, so a value describes the planet over a period, not the ionosphere above one receiver. The scale is quasi logarithmic and published in thirds of a unit. Storm levels start at 5 (G1), Kp stops at 9, and Hp30 keeps climbing past it in an extreme storm. Fixes whose day is not in the geomagnetic index archive carry no value.
